undraising while Shapiro funds downballot Democrats"], "rationale": "Polling from May through September consistently shows Shapiro up 17-25 points, including a +20 result from NYT/Siena in late September, and raters across the spectrum unanimously rate the race Solid or Safe Democratic. Markets price his odds near 97%, and Pennsylvania's slight Republican lean is outweighed by his incumbency strength and Garrity's weak name recognition and fundraising.", "watch": "A sharply nationalized midterm environment favoring Republicans, a late-breaking negative story, or an unexpectedly strong Libertarian showing could narrow the margin.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Josh Shapiro (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Josh Shapiro seeks a second term against Republican Stacy Garrity, with Libertarian Ken Krawchuk also on the ballot. Every major poll since spring shows Shapiro leading by double digits, with the most recent high-quality surveys putting the margin near 20 points. Rating outlets across the spectrum call the race solidly Democratic, and prediction markets price Shapiro's chances around 97%.\n\nGarrity has struggled with name recognition and fundraising, while Shapiro has used his incumbency and campaign resources to support downballot Democrats. Pennsylvania's slight Republican lean in federal races has not translated into a competitive governor's contest this cycle. The main uncertainty is whether late-breaking events or a nationalized political climate could tighten the race, but current evidence points to a comfortable Shapiro re-election.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 15.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}